  "checks": [
    {
      "area": "Permanent owner versus temporary restrictions",
      "result": "MainOwner live state is shared only by Bound Rc<Owner>;50ms observer tests weak Main upgrade failure, not visibility/question/chooser state. Temporary hide or exit question therefore preserves draft. valid_callback separately prevents writes immediately when Main dies, before poll closure. Final Bound clone drop runs Owner::drop; nonfinal clones keep owner alive.",
      "source": [
        "predicate_editor_window.rs:26-109",
        "lib.rs:298-299,441-442,603-609"
      ]
    },
    {
      "area": "Weak timer/callback ownership",
      "result": "Timer callback, valid_callback and retire_callback each capture Weak<MainOwner>. Main parent is slint::Weak. No callback retains Rc<Owner>, so external window/collector callbacks cannot keep final Bound owner alive; no self-timer/slot/parent Rc cycle identified. MainOwner owns its slot, and existing child close holds weak slot/window. Timer stops once retirement begins.",
      "source": [
        "predicate_editor_window.rs:26-109,497-524",
        "lib.rs:715-751,3361-3411"
      ]
    },
    {
      "area": "Borrow and reentrancy safety",
      "result": "retire marks livefalse/stops timer and clones exact current child into local; RefCell borrow ends before invoke_cancel. Existing close marks closed once, hides child, checks exact window-slot identity with released read borrow before take, then cancels notices. Notices::cancel similarly clones close callback before invoking it. No RefCell borrow held across child/notice cancellation and no second retirement mutation identified.",
      "source": [
        "predicate_editor_window.rs:34-50,497-524",
        "predicate_notice.rs:28-36,55-75"
      ]
    },
    {
      "area": "Main creation and existing-edit admission",
      "result": "Main bind constructs owner and shares weak valid gate with new system launch + per-editor owner and active-predicate binder. Accepted exit and rebind invoke weak retire callback; bind retires old binding before successor setup. All active callback.get sites changed consistently to Fn invocation; one bind caller found. Existing selected-page/lock/visibility/question guards stay.",
      "source": [
        "lib.rs:584-610,1217-1232,1475-1549,3361-3411",
        "active_predicates.rs:125-169,230-245,355-383"
      ]
    },
    {
      "area": "Stale callbacks and successor safety",
      "result": "Old state holds its old slot, never successor slot; terminal livefalse + existing closed flag reject mutations/default/recent/query publication, even if retained component manually reshown. Existing close uses pointer identity before clearing slot; closed/notice alive flags are once-only. Rebind timer is stopped; weak expired old callback cannot retire new state.",
      "source": [
        "predicate_editor_window.rs:34-109,352-360,497-552",
        "predicate_notice.rs:55-90",
        "filesize_predicate.rs:372-485"
      ]
    },
    {
      "area": "Meaningful automatic destruction tests",
      "result": "New-size and existing-size tests hide/drop only Main, assert WeakMain None, retain Bound/child/collector, pump real timers<=2s and require slotNone/childhidden. No child Cancel/hide or collector release precedes automatic closure. Existing-size test also preserves exact Vec<HashId> membership (page.files returns flattened IDs). Size clone test proves nonfinal Bound live/editable then final Bound terminal and successor accepted123KB. Hash loops Main death with Bound retained and final Bound drop with Main retained, requires BOTH editor/notice hidden and notice flags cleared. Retained stale actions and reopened Store defaults/recent remain unchanged.",
      "source": [
        "filesize_predicate.rs:305-485",
        "active_predicates.rs:1139-1239",
        "hash_predicate.rs:379-517",
        "page.rs:2063-2066"
      ]
